+++ b/features/clear-completed.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@
+Feature: Clear completed
+  As a user
+  I want to remove all completed todos at once
+  So that I can clean up my list
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed removes all completed todos
+    Given the user has created a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user has created a todo "Walk the dog"
+    And the user has created a todo "Buy milk"
+    And the todo "Buy groceries" is completed
+    And the todo "Walk the dog" is completed
+    When the user clicks the clear completed button
+    Then the todo "Buy groceries" should not exist in the list
+    And the todo "Walk the dog" should not exist in the list
+    And the todo "Buy milk" should exist in the list
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed button is hidden when no completed todos exist
+    Given the user has created a todo "Buy groceries"
+    Then the clear completed button should be hidden
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed button is shown when completed todos exist
+    Given the user has created a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the todo "Buy groceries" is completed
+    Then the clear completed button should be visible
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed with all todos completed hides main and footer
+    Given the user has created a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the todo "Buy groceries" is completed
+    When the user clicks the clear completed button
+    Then the main section should be hidden
+    And the footer should be hidden
diff --git a/features/counter.feature b/features/counter.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..ada5282
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/counter.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+Feature: Counter
+  As a user
+  I want to see how many active todos remain
+  So that I can track my remaining work
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Scenario: Counter shows zero items when no todos exist
+    Then the counter should show "0 items left"
+
+  Scenario: Counter shows singular for one active todo
+    Given the user has created a todo "Buy groceries"
+    Then the counter should show "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: Counter shows plural for multiple active todos
+    Given the user has created a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user has created a todo "Walk the dog"
+    Then the counter should show "2 items left"
+
+  Scenario: Counter only counts active todos
+    Given the user has created a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user has created a todo "Walk the dog"
+    And the todo "Buy groceries" is completed
+    Then the counter should show "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: Counter updates when a todo is completed
+    Given the user has created a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user has created a todo "Walk the dog"
+    When the user completes the todo "Buy groceries"
+    Then the counter should show "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: Counter updates when a completed todo is uncompleted
+    Given the user has created a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the todo "Buy groceries" is completed
+    When the user uncompletes the todo "Buy groceries"
+    Then the counter should show "1 item left"
diff --git a/features/editing.feature b/features/editing.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..4fd524f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/editing.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,52 @@
+Feature: Editing
+  As a user
+  I want to edit existing todos
+  So that I can correct or update their titles
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Scenario: Saving an edit on blur
+    Given the user has created a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the todo "Buy groceries" is in editing mode
+    When the user types "Buy milk" in the edit input
+    And the edit input loses focus
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" should exist in the list
+    And the todo "Buy groceries" should not exist in the list
+
+  Scenario: Saving an edit on Enter
+    Given the user has created a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the todo "Buy groceries" is in editing mode
+    When the user types "Buy milk" in the edit input
+    And the user presses Enter
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" should exist in the list
+    And the todo "Buy groceries" should not exist in the list
+
+  Scenario: Cancelling an edit on Escape
+    Given the user has created a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the todo "Buy groceries" is in editing mode
+    When the user types "Buy milk" in the edit input
+    And the user presses Escape
+    Then the todo "Buy groceries" should exist in the list
+    And the todo "Buy milk" should not exist in the list
+
+  Scenario: Editing an empty title destroys the todo
+    Given the user has created a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the todo "Buy groceries" is in editing mode
+    When the user clears the edit input
+    And the edit input loses focus
+    Then no todo should exist in the list
+
+  Scenario: Editing to whitespace-only destroys the todo
+    Given the user has created a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the todo "Buy groceries" is in editing mode
+    When the user types "   " in the edit input
+    And the edit input loses focus
+    Then no todo should exist in the list
+
+  Scenario: Editing is trimmed before saving
+    Given the user has created a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the todo "Buy groceries" is in editing mode
+    When the user types "  Buy milk  " in the edit input
+    And the user presses Enter
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" should exist in the list
