+++ b/features/routing.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,51 @@
+Feature: Routing
+  As a user
+  I want to filter my todos by status
+  So that I can focus on active or completed items
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Scenario: All filter shows all todos
+    Given the user has created a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user has created a todo "Walk the dog"
+    And the todo "Buy groceries" is completed
+    When the user navigates to "#/"
+    Then the todo "Buy groceries" should be visible
+    And the todo "Walk the dog" should be visible
+    And the "All" filter should be selected
+
+  Scenario: Active filter shows only active todos
+    Given the user has created a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user has created a todo "Walk the dog"
+    And the todo "Buy groceries" is completed
+    When the user navigates to "#/active"
+    Then the todo "Buy groceries" should not be visible
+    And the todo "Walk the dog" should be visible
+    And the "Active" filter should be selected
+
+  Scenario: Completed filter shows only completed todos
+    Given the user has created a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user has created a todo "Walk the dog"
+    And the todo "Buy groceries" is completed
+    When the user navigates to "#/completed"
+    Then the todo "Buy groceries" should be visible
+    And the todo "Walk the dog" should not be visible
+    And the "Completed" filter should be selected
+
+  Scenario: Completing a todo while on active filter hides it
+    Given the user has created a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user has created a todo "Walk the dog"
+    And the user navigates to "#/active"
+    When the user completes the todo "Buy groceries"
+    Then the todo "Buy groceries" should not be visible
+    And the todo "Walk the dog" should be visible
+
+  Scenario: Uncompleting a todo while on completed filter hides it
+    Given the user has created a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the user has created a todo "Walk the dog"
+    And the todo "Buy groceries" is completed
+    And the user navigates to "#/completed"
+    When the user uncompletes the todo "Buy groceries"
+    Then the todo "Buy groceries" should not be visible
+    And the todo "Walk the dog" should not be visible
diff --git a/features/todo-item.feature b/features/todo-item.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..b1b6811
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todo-item.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+Feature: Todo item
+  As a user
+  I want to interact with individual todo items
+  So that I can mark them complete, edit them, and delete them
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Scenario: Clicking checkbox marks a todo as completed
+    Given the user has created a todo "Buy groceries"
+    When the user completes the todo "Buy groceries"
+    Then the todo "Buy groceries" should be completed
+
+  Scenario: Unchecking a completed todo marks it as active
+    Given the user has created a todo "Buy groceries"
+    And the todo "Buy groceries" is completed
+    When the user uncompletes the todo "Buy groceries"
+    Then the todo "Buy groceries" should not be completed
+
+  Scenario: Double-clicking a todo label activates editing
+    Given the user has created a todo "Buy groceries"
+    When the user double-clicks the todo "Buy groceries"
+    Then the todo "Buy groceries" should be in editing mode
+    And the edit input should contain "Buy groceries"
+    And the edit input should be focused
+
+  Scenario: Clicking destroy button removes the todo
+    Given the user has created a todo "Buy groceries"
+    When the user destroys the todo "Buy groceries"
+    Then no todo should exist in the list
+    And the main section should be hidden
+    And the footer should be hidden
+
+  Scenario: Completed todos have completed class
+    Given the user has created a todo "Buy groceries"
+    When the user completes the todo "Buy groceries"
+    Then the todo "Buy groceries" should have the "completed" class
diff --git a/features/toggle-all.feature b/features/toggle-all.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..516d3a5
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/toggle-all.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@
+Feature: Toggle all
+  As a user
+  I want to mark all todos as complete at once
+  So that I can quickly complete everything
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Scenario: Toggle all marks every todo as completed
+    Given the user has created a todo "First"
+    And the user has created a todo "Second"
+    When the user clicks the toggle-all checkbox
+    Then the todo "First" should be completed
+    And the todo "Second" should be completed
+
+  Scenario: Toggle all unmarks every todo when all are completed
+    Given the user has created a todo "First"
+    And the user has created a todo "Second"
+    And all todos are completed
+    When the user clicks the toggle-all checkbox
+    Then the todo "First" should not be completed
+    And the todo "Second" should not be completed
+
+  Scenario: Toggle all reflects state when individual todos are toggled
+    Given the user has created a todo "First"
+    And the user has created a todo "Second"
+    When the user completes the todo "First"
+    Then the toggle-all checkbox should not be checked
+    When the user completes the todo "Second"
+    Then the toggle-all checkbox should be checked
+
+  Scenario: Toggle all clears after clear completed is clicked
+    Given the user has created a todo "First"
+    And the user has created a todo "Second"
+    And all todos are completed
+    When the user clicks the toggle-all checkbox
+    And the user clicks the clear completed button
+    Then the main section should be hidden
+    And the footer should be hidden
